cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite both the code
  (this repository) and the associated article listed under
  "preferred-citation".
title: >-
  Analysis and figure code for "Hidden motor neuron activity restores grasp
  in children with paralysed hand"
abstract: >-
  Analysis and figure-generation code accompanying the study "Hidden motor
  neuron activity restores grasp in children with paralysed hand".
  Includes the high-density surface-EMG figure scripts (Figure 2, Figure 3) and
  the Figure 4 offline-decoding pipeline (rule-based attempt labelling,
  leave-one-repetition-out CatBoost cross-validation, permutation statistics,
  Figure 4, Supplementary Figures S2b-S7b and Supplementary Table S2). To
  protect the vulnerable paediatric participants, no participant data —
  neither the raw recordings nor any derived features — are distributed
  with this software; all data are available from the authors on reasonable
  request. The code is provided so that the methodology is fully transparent and
  the results can be reproduced once data access has been granted.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-08
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21269465
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/NsquaredLab/IntuitivePeripheralDecodingRestoresHandControlAfterChildhoodHemispherotomy/
keywords:
  - electromyography
  - EMG
  - hemispherotomy
  - early brain lesions
  - motor decoding
  - myocontrol
  - gesture classification
  - motor units
  - neurorehabilitation
